1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:01,880
My eternal gratitude.
我永恒的感激之情。

2
00:00:02,360 --> 00:00:12,300
And I look out into the crowd, and I see people who worked for me on my very first campaign for Congress back and
我向人群望去，看到了在我第一次竞选国会时为我工作的人

3
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:13,520
That's a long time ago.
那是很久以前的事了。

4
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:18,620
It's back when only birds tweeted and TikTok came from a clock.
那时还只有鸟儿会“推特”，TikTok 还只是时钟的滴答声。

5
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:19,940
It was a long time ago.
那是很久以前的事了。

6
00:00:20,460 --> 00:00:21,700
So I thank all of you.
所以我感谢你们所有人。

7
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:33,534
And to my phenomenal campaign team, with deep thanks to Stacy Monahan and [name unclear], and our campaign manager [name unclear],
还有我出色的竞选团队，特别感谢斯泰西·莫纳汉和[姓名不清]，以及我们的竞选经理[姓名不清]，

8
00:00:34,060 --> 00:00:36,520
You fought hard every single day.
你们每一天都在努力奋斗。

9
00:00:36,980 --> 00:00:41,360
You did so magnificently and you cared so deeply.
你做得如此出色，你如此深切地关心。

10
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:54,133
You left it all out on the field and we won and tonight we celebrate because tomorrow we have work to do to to
你把一切都留在了球场上，我们赢了，今晚我们庆祝，因为明天我们还有工作要做

11
00:00:54,133 --> 00:00:56,380
To save our democracy.
为了拯救我们的民主。

12
00:00:56,380 --> 00:01:01,580
We don't know yet the full outcome of today's elections around the country,
我们还不知道今天全国各地选举的全部结果，

13
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:11,200
But we do know that Donald Trump is the most corrupt, the most desperate person to ever lead our country.
但我们确实知道唐纳德·特朗普是有史以来领导我们国家的最腐败、最绝望的人。

14
00:01:12,060 --> 00:01:18,020
He every day in the Oval Office he is a walking, talking constitutional crisis.
他每天在椭圆形办公室里行走、谈论宪法危机。

15
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:25,740
He and his maga Republican enablers know they can't win on the issues.
他和他的共和党支持者知道他们无法在这些问题上获胜。

16
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:27,180
How could they?
他们怎么能呢？

17
00:01:27,180 --> 00:01:36,600
Gas prices are up, grocery prices are up, tariffs are up, healthcare premiums are up,
汽油价格上涨，杂货价格上涨，关税上涨，医疗保费上涨，

18
00:01:36,980 --> 00:01:39,840
And the anger of American voters are up.
美国选民的愤怒也在上升。

19
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:42,620
So what are they trying to do today?
那么他们今天想做什么？

20
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:43,720
Cheat.
欺骗。

21
00:01:44,220 --> 00:01:52,700
Baseless lawsuits to kick voters off the rolls, threats to use nuclear weapons in Iran after the election,
毫无根据的诉讼将选民踢出名单，选举后威胁在伊朗使用核武器，

22
00:01:53,240 --> 00:02:02,380
Violent ICE agents patrolling the streets for months to keep our immigrant fearful and at home.
暴力的 ICE 特工在街道上巡逻了数月，让我们的移民感到恐惧并留在家里。

23
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:11,220
The President may try to steal the election, but he has no say whatsoever in the conduct of elections.
总统可能会试图窃取选举结果，但他对选举的进行没有任何发言权。

24
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:16,220
I guess they did not teach that at Trump University.
我猜他们在特朗普大学没有教过这个。

25
00:02:18,206 --> 00:02:26,350
We will make sure that our elections are free and fair and not bought and paid for,
我们将确保我们的选举是自由和公平的，而不是花钱买来的，

26
00:02:26,770 --> 00:02:33,210
But we cannot respond to this moment with cynicism or with resignation for the poor,
但我们不能以愤世嫉俗或对穷人的顺从来应对这一时刻，

27
00:02:33,510 --> 00:02:35,470
The sick, the elderly.
病人、老人。

28
00:02:36,050 --> 00:02:40,490
The past is just a memory, and the future is their hard reality.
过去只是记忆，未来才是他们的残酷现实。

29
00:02:40,918 --> 00:02:50,290
The solution to despair is the courage to fight back and the hope that comes from exercising that power.
解决绝望的方法是反击的勇气和运用这种力量带来的希望。

30
00:02:50,730 --> 00:02:55,370
And I'm thinking of the phone banks at Ula Cafe in Jamaica Plain,
我想到了牙买加平原乌拉咖啡馆的电话银行，

31
00:02:55,370 --> 00:03:08,844
Where dozens of people are calling members of Congress to extend temporary protected status for Haitian tps holders.
数十人呼吁国会议员延长海地临时保护身份持有者的临时保护地位。

32
00:03:10,092 --> 00:03:15,472
And I'm thinking of the neighbors and advocates who are giving big checks,
我想到的是那些提供大额支票的邻居和倡导者，

33
00:03:15,472 --> 00:03:17,660
The big finger on polluting data centers.
对污染数据中心的大手笔。

34
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:23,740
No community should have a data center if they don't want it.
如果社区不想要的话，就不应该拥有数据中心。

35
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:28,820
They should have the right to say no.
他们应该有权说不。

36
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:32,520
The American people did not sign up for this.
美国人民并没有对此表示同意。

37
00:03:33,016 --> 00:03:40,300
You can't gut Medicaid by a trillion dollars and then give a trillion dollar tax break to billionaires.
你不可能削减一万亿美元的医疗补助，然后给亿万富翁提供一万亿美元的税收减免。

38
00:03:40,540 --> 00:03:43,780
Tonight, we say no more.
今晚，我们不再多说。

39
00:03:44,080 --> 00:03:53,900
When Republicans gas holes in our social safety net, we will be the ones to mend the fabric hole again.
当共和党人给我们的社会安全网造成漏洞时，我们将再次修补这个漏洞。

40
00:03:53,900 --> 00:04:00,920
When they undermine our democratic institutions, we will uphold the rule of law.
当他们破坏我们的民主制度时，我们将维护法治。

41
00:04:01,340 --> 00:04:08,300
And when they try to silence those who speak out against them, we will meet them in the courts.
当他们试图压制那些公开反对他们的人时，我们将在法庭上与他们会面。

42
00:04:08,496 --> 00:04:16,200
We will meet them in the streets, and we will bring a soapbox and a bullhorn and a box of receipts,
我们会在街上遇见他们，我们会带上一个肥皂盒、一个扩音器和一盒收据，

43
00:04:16,394 --> 00:04:18,440
And we will win.
我们会赢。

44
00:04:23,150 --> 00:04:28,910
Because on every issue, we are right and Trump is wrong.
因为在每个问题上，我们都是对的，特朗普都是错的。

45
00:04:30,518 --> 00:04:36,180
We can watch the darkness grow and give up, or we can fix it.
我们可以看着黑暗增长并放弃，或者我们可以修复它。

46
00:04:36,740 --> 00:04:39,140
But only if we meet this moment together.
但前提是我们一起迎接这一刻。

47
00:04:39,860 --> 00:04:45,860
As Dr. King said, that only when it is dark enough can you see the stars.
正如金博士所说，只有当天足够黑时，你才能看到星星。

48
00:04:46,894 --> 00:04:52,040
Our democracy is threatened, but it will endure because of you, the stars.
我们的民主受到威胁，但由于你们，星星，它将会持续下去。

49
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:58,860
Our democracy is stronger than greed and corruption because you are stronger than that.
我们的民主比贪婪和腐败更强大，因为你们比它们更强大。

50
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:07,940
Our democracy is more resilient than the chest-thumping threats of a petty tyrant because you are more resilient than that.
我们的民主比小暴君的重重威胁更有弹性，因为你比那更有弹性。

51
00:05:08,512 --> 00:05:14,880
We in Massachusetts say no kings, not 250 years ago and not now.
我们马萨诸塞州说没有国王，250 年前不是，现在也不是。

52
00:05:15,220 --> 00:05:17,540
No kings movement started here.
这里没有国王运动开始。

53
00:05:19,054 --> 00:05:31,990
And our democracy, our democracy has more potential than the injustice and hate of Donald Trump and his racist, Xenophobic ICE thugs.
我们的民主，我们的民主比唐纳德·特朗普及其种族主义者的不公正和仇恨更有潜力，仇外的 ICE 暴徒。

54
00:05:32,490 --> 00:05:36,411
We must abolish ICE now.
我们现在必须废除 ICE。

55
00:05:38,638 --> 00:05:43,084
We are stronger.
我们更强大。

56
00:05:43,084 --> 00:05:45,580
We are stronger because of our diversity.
我们因我们的多样性而变得更强大。

57
00:05:45,900 --> 00:05:53,320
We are a nation of immigrants who built this country, and they deserve a pathway to citizenship.
我们是一个由移民组成的国家，他们建立了这个国家，他们应该有一条获得公民身份的途径。

58
00:05:53,820 --> 00:06:01,400
But the fight, the fight to protect and rebuild our democracy won't take just some of us.
但这场保护和重建民主的斗争不仅仅需要我们中的一些人。

59
00:06:01,540 --> 00:06:03,920
It will take all of us.
这需要我们所有人。

60
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:10,560
And that is I am hopeful in this moment, when there is so much fear and hate,
这就是我在这一刻充满希望，当有如此多的恐惧和仇恨时，

61
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:17,940
That is why I am optimistic because there are more of us than there are of them.
这就是为什么我很乐观，因为我们的人数比他们的人数还要多。

62
00:06:18,221 --> 00:06:33,380
Because when we stand together with better ideas and stronger ideals, they don't stand a chance because the many will always beat the money Every single time.
因为当我们与更好的想法和更坚定的理想站在一起时，他们就没有机会，因为多数人总是会打败金钱每一次。

63
00:06:36,995 --> 00:06:42,650
Massachusetts runs on Dunkin's, but we also run on resistance.
马萨诸塞州靠唐恩都乐提神，也靠坚持抗争前行。

64
00:06:43,330 --> 00:06:48,550
My father, a union leader, taught me you don't beg for your rights,
我的父亲是一名工会领袖，他教导我不要乞求自己的权利，

65
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:51,070
You organize and you take them.
你组织并接受它们。

66
00:06:51,342 --> 00:06:53,270
Our work is not done tonight.
今晚我们的工作还没有完成。

67
00:06:53,750 --> 00:06:58,850
There is an epic fight before us in the weeks ahead in January with a new Congress,
在接下来的一月份的几周里，我们将与新一届国会展开一场史诗般的战斗，

68
00:06:58,850 --> 00:07:07,785
And until we get Donald Trump out of the White House and we make GOP stand for get out and we make GOP stand
直到我们让唐纳德·特朗普离开白宫，我们让共和党人代表滚蛋，我们让共和党人代表

69
00:07:07,785 --> 00:07:12,998
For get out permanently.
为了永久退出。

70
00:07:14,495 --> 00:07:19,040
And that is because we don't agonize, we organize.
那是因为我们不苦恼，我们组织。

71
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:26,000
And every day, every day we organize for our democracy to reclaim it,
每一天，每一天我们都组织起来争取我们的民主，以夺回它，

72
00:07:26,300 --> 00:07:34,340
To rebuild it so that every child, every family can have the chance to dream and to realize a better future.
重建它，让每个孩子、每个家庭都有机会梦想并实现更美好的未来。

73
00:07:34,340 --> 00:07:39,620
We organize because we believe in something so big that it cannot be stopped.
我们组织起来是因为我们相信一些大到无法阻止的事情。

74
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:41,800
We believe in the power of the people.
我们相信人民的力量。

75
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:46,369
We believe in Medicare for all and health care as a human right.
我们相信全民医疗保险和医疗保健是一项人权。

76
00:07:49,410 --> 00:07:52,290
We believe in streets free from gun violence.
我们相信街道上没有枪支暴力。

77
00:07:54,210 --> 00:07:59,690
We believe in a world without war, and we believe in the unrelenting push for peace.
我们相信世界可以没有战争，也相信应当坚持不懈地争取和平。

78
00:07:59,690 --> 00:08:04,090
We believe in civil rights and LGBTQ rights.
我们相信公民权利和 LGBTQ 权利。

79
00:08:04,690 --> 00:08:10,500
We believe that trans rights are human rights.
我们相信跨性别者的权利就是人权。

80
00:08:15,020 --> 00:08:21,680
And the Congress needs to pass my trans bill of rights.
国会需要通过我的跨性别权利法案。

81
00:08:23,700 --> 00:08:33,630
A livable wage, reproductive freedom, universal childcare, paid sick leave for all workers,
足以维持生计的工资、生育自由、全民儿童保育、所有工人的带薪病假、

82
00:08:34,130 --> 00:08:41,050
Free community college, free public college, a green new deal now.
免费社区大学，免费公立大学，现在是绿色新政。

83
00:08:45,997 --> 00:08:53,020
An end to the illegal and immoral war in Iran and an end to bombing in gaza.
结束伊朗非法和不道德的战争，结束加沙的轰炸。

84
00:08:54,486 --> 00:09:04,040
We must recommit to education, not we must recommit to education, not annihilation.
我们必须重新致力于教育，而不是我们必须重新致力于教育，而不是消灭。

85
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:10,900
This must be our agenda, our progressive agenda in the next Congress.
这必须成为我们的议程，我们在下届国会中的进步议程。

86
00:09:11,995 --> 00:09:12,587
Yes.
是的。

87
00:09:12,587 --> 00:09:18,460
Most national election results are still coming in this evening, but no matter the outcome,
大多数全国选举结果仍将在今晚公布，但无论结果如何，

88
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:20,740
I am never giving up.
我永远不会放弃。

89
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:24,900
You are never giving up on our Massachusetts values.
您永远不会放弃我们马萨诸塞州的价值观。

90
00:09:25,320 --> 00:09:30,880
And I know I am surrounded by people who feel the very same way.
我知道我周围的人都有同样的感觉。

91
00:09:31,420 --> 00:09:34,260
A new day is rising in America.
美国新的一天即将来临。

92
00:09:34,771 --> 00:09:37,180
It's And it's ours for the taking.
这是我们的。

93
00:09:37,180 --> 00:09:43,160
If we have the resolve to seize it together, we will create a healthier,
如果我们有决心共同抓住它，我们将创造一个更健康、

94
00:09:43,540 --> 00:09:48,840
Fairer, more prosperous, peaceful, and hope-filled future for everyone.
为每个人带来更公平、更繁荣、更和平、更充满希望的未来。

95
00:09:49,420 --> 00:09:50,820
I'm Senator Ed Markey.
我是参议员埃德·马基。

96
00:09:51,300 --> 00:09:56,640
It is the honor of my life to represent the Commonwealth of Massachusetts in the United States Senate.
我一生很荣幸能够在美国参议院代表马萨诸塞州。

97
00:09:57,200 --> 00:10:02,000
We have got a fight ahead, and you haven't seen anything yet.
我们前面有一场战斗，而你还没有看到任何东西。

98
00:10:02,380 --> 00:10:04,129
Thank you, Massachusetts.
谢谢你，马萨诸塞州。

99
00:10:04,129 --> 00:10:04,760
Thank you.
谢谢你。
